{"name":"Dusty Trail Rider","hex":"#c3b9a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with dust.","Powdery and resembling dust."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A medium-brown color.","An old bottle of spirits that has been kept for a long time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusty"},{"term":"trail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To follow behind (someone or something); to tail (someone or something).","To drag (something) behind on the ground."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The track or indication marking the route followed by something that has passed, such as the footprints of animal on land or the contrail of an airplane in the sky.","A route for travel over land, especially a narrow, unpaved pathway for use by hikers, horseback riders, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail"},{"term":"rider","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mounted person.\n A knight, or other mounted warrior. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\nAn old Dutch gold coin with the figure of a man on horseback stamped upon it. \n\n Someone who rides a horse or (later) a bicycle, motorcycle etc. \n\n A motorcycle enthusiast; a motorcycle club member.\n A mounted robber; a bandit, especially in the Scottish borders. \n\n Someone who breaks in or manages a horse; a riding master. \n\n An agent who goes out with samples of goods to obtain orders; a commercial traveller or travelling salesman. \n\n  Someone riding in a vehicle; a passenger on public transport. \n\n A boarder, a person who rides a board in boardsports.\n A skateboarder\n\n A snowboarder","A knight, or other mounted warrior. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rider"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Trail Rider","blocks":[{"text":"The Trail Rider is a 1925 American silent Western film directed by W. S. Van Dyke and starring Buck Jones. Based on the 1924 novel The Trail Rider: A Romance of the Kansas Range by George Washington Ogden, the film is about a trail rider hired to protect ranchers from the actions of a corrupt banker. The film was produced by Fox Film Corp. and was released on February 22, 1925, in the United States. It marked Gary Cooper’s film debut as a stunt rider. It is not known whether the film currently survives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/The_Trail_Rider_%281925%29_poster.jpg/330px-The_Trail_Rider_%281925%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Trail_Rider"},{"title":"Trail","blocks":[{"text":"A trail, also known as a path or track, is a dirt road or a small paved road, usually through an undeveloped natural area, that is designed primarily for use by pedestrians, equestrians and non-motorized vehicles, although occasionally some off-roading motor vehicles may also use it. In the United Kingdom and Ireland, footpath or hiking trail is the preferred term. However, it is sometimes applied to highways in North America. In the United States, the term was historically used to describe the westward expansion trails, which are land routes into or through wildness regions of the American West used by explorers and migrants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg/330px-Trail_between_two_fields_%28Slovenia%2C_Selo_pri_Mirni%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/MountainBikeTrail.jpg/500px-MountainBikeTrail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/MountainBikeTrail.jpg/1280px-MountainBikeTrail.jpg?utm_source=